##Mini Project

##Project Description

# This project integrates a two-wheel motor control system with a computer vision interface using a Raspberry Pi and Arduino. 
# A camera detects the position of a visual marker within four image quadrants, and the marker location is used to command independent 
# target positions for the left and right wheels. The system also implements PI position control so the motors return to their commanded 
# positions after disturbances, while an LCD displays the current goal positions.

##How to Run
# To run this code, plug in the rasberryPI into the ardunio as awell as connect a mouse, powersource, and camera to the Pi (keyboard optional)
# make sure both lights are green on the ardunio and PI by turning on the robot, this will include flipping the switch on the robot to 1
# upload the Arduino code to the Ardunio by verifying it then pressing the upload button. 
# once that is done press run in the Python code. Move around the ID

##Files
#arucoDetect: Coding portion for the pi
#arduinoCode: Coding portion of the arduino (with inigration of receiving pi info)
#tmp_mini_demo.ino: Coding portion of the arduino (without pi intigration)
